{
  "tableVersion": 2,
  "recorded": "2026-11-20",
  "current_release": "v0.8.0",
  "note": "Cross-repo pin reference table for the toolkit, in the five classes of FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#241 plus the copied-tree class added by FAIR-bioHeaders-Tools#163. Each row records what this repository asserts: `sha256` and `bytes` are the digest and size of the pinned bytes, `local` is the vendored copy in this checkout, and `repository`, `revision` and `path` name the authoritative bytes to compare with - a tag for anything released, a commit for a draft contract or a suite. A `copied-tree` row instead names a consumer provenance record (`provenance`, located under `consumer` relative to --root) whose `copied[]` entries give the per-path digests; a consumer with no such record reports ABSENT, because absence is the finding. `bioheaders-pin-audit` reads this table and reports FRESH / DRIFT / ABSENT per row; it is data, not prose, reading it never writes it, and changing a value is a deliberate, dated commit. A row with no digest is a documented hole and reports ABSENT. A row with no digest is a documented hole; filling one is a deliberate, dated commit: the FHGM draft axes added here (#135) replace the `fhgm-base@none` hole with the pinned record contract, transport overlay, base registry, two released bases and the development suite.",
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Dockerfile:17 pins the python:3.13-slim base image by digest, and release.yml and container.yml pin released toolkit bytes: container and package-version references, not contract bytes.",
    "plugins/ and galaxy/ version tokens follow the package version and are checked by tests/claude_plugin_test.py and .github/workflows/galaxy-tools.yml.",
    "fhr/ and the top-level compatibility copies mirror files inside this repository, so they are same-repo copies, not cross-repo references."
  ],
